Add a one-way, timelocked, deny-only narrowing. It extends the admin's writes beyond PRD 13 and 14's remove-only wording (D-014 and B2-8/9 already did that), so it needs the owner's sign-off and a DECISIONS entry.

```solidity
event SessionTypeNarrowed(uint8 indexed id, address indexed token);
error SessionTypeNotNarrowable(uint8 id, SessionCalendar.SessionType sessionType);

/// @notice Moves an ALL_DAY ticker to REGULAR for good (research Q2).
/// @dev Caller: the timelock.
function narrowSessionType(uint8 id) external onlyTimelock {
    Ticker storage entry = _ticker(id);
    if (entry.sessionType != SessionCalendar.SessionType.ALL_DAY) revert SessionTypeNotNarrowable(id, entry.sessionType);
    entry.sessionType = SessionCalendar.SessionType.REGULAR;
    emit SessionTypeNarrowed(id, entry.token);
}
```

The module needs no change, because _guard, previews and sessionOpenedAt read the type on every call.

